# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Compiled Go command binaries built at repo root (extensionless on Linux, so
# the *.exe/*.so patterns above don't catch them — listed explicitly, anchored
# so identically-named subdirs/packages are unaffected).
/app
/boxer
/envgen
/imzero2
/licensegate

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work

# goland files
.idea

# Local analysis outputs at repo root (anchored so subdirs are unaffected).
/report.md
/summary.md
/assessment.gen.md
/out.json
/results.json

# Local planning / scratch notes at repo root (e.g. PLAN-*.md working docs).
# Anchored so identically-named files in subdirs are unaffected.
/PLAN-*.md

# Rust build artifacts — cargo target directories under rust/<crate>/target.
rust/*/target/

# Airgap build bundles produced at repo root by airgap-bundle.sh (ADR-0095):
# the tarball (boxer-airgap-<scope>-<arch>-<date>.tar.zst, or .tar.gz with the
# gzip fallback) ships toolchains + vendored sources and must not be committed.
# Anchored so identically-suffixed files in subdirs are unaffected.
/boxer-airgap-*.tar.zst
/boxer-airgap-*.tar.gz

# Codec source tarballs + build tree for the bundled static ffmpeg
# (airgap_ship_ffmpeg -> build-static-ffmpeg.sh). Cached at repo root across
# packs so a re-pack does not re-download ~89 MB; only the linked binary is
# shipped. Never committed.
/.airgap-ffmpeg-src/

# Pinned upstream release tarballs the bundle ships prebuilt (tinygo). Cached at
# repo root across packs — ~170 MB — and re-verified against the SHA-256 pins in
# airgap-lib.sh on every use. Never committed.
/.airgap-dl/

# boxer adr tool cache — the `boxer adr build` default --out dir. It can be
# created in any working directory (the command takes --root), so not anchored.
.adrcache/

# The competence vault (ADR-0168 §SD7) — the business-capability corpus. It is
# present in a working tree but unversioned: which catalogs may be published,
# and under what licence, is not settled, and committing the tree now would
# decide that by accident. Only the README is tracked — it says what belongs
# here.
/doc/competences/*
!/doc/competences/README.md

# Local Claude Code settings (machine-specific); the .claude/skills symlink stays tracked.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Local `crush` agent config (machine-specific): points at a localhost model
# server, so it is developer-environment state, not shared project config.
# Anchored — the repo-root file only.
/crush.json

# Scratch output from the dev capture scripts — scripts/dev/play-screenshot-tour.sh
# and scripts/dev/tree-widget-scene.sh default their OUT here, and each builds a
# private Go host and Rust client into it (>100 MB a run).
/tmp/

# The binary boxer.sh builds. It names it after `mktemp` and realpaths that
# basename into the repo root, and removes it on exit — so one only survives a
# run that was killed, at ~120 MB each. Anchored: repo root only.
/tmp.*

# ClickHouse server state, written into the working directory by a server
# started from the repo root: the config it expands on start, and the access
# lists it keeps beside it.
/preprocessed_configs/
/access/

# A hand-run wasm compile check (a main.go and its ~7 MB out.wasm), kept
# between probes rather than rebuilt. Scratch, not a fixture.
/.manual-probe/

# rapid's counterexample files, written under a package's testdata/rapid/ when
# a property test fails. Each records one local run; a regression worth keeping
# belongs in a test, not here. `**/` because the pattern would otherwise anchor
# to the repo root, where no package lives.
**/testdata/rapid/

# the lading snapshot mountpoint (doc/howto/lading-snapshot-store.md §6):
# ignored so doclint and the gov gate do not walk a mounted snapshot as if it
# were repo source.
/tally/
